DOCS_FRAGMENT("part:birth-settlement-sk", "<p class=\"lede partlede\">A Slovak or Subcarpathian birth to one 1910 GISta settlement: the gazetteer and its Majo join, tiers, refusals, repairs, residuals. · source: <code>reference/BIRTH_SETTLEMENT_SK.md</code></p><div class=\"sheetroot\" id=\"sheet-birth-settlement-sk\"><div class=\"tldr\"><div class=\"tldr-h\">In short</div><p>A Slovak or Subcarpathian birth is placed twice. The <strong>district step</strong> reads the district string and puts the birth\nin a 1910 <strong>járás</strong>, through a Magyar↔Slovak dictionary. The <strong>settlement link</strong> then reads the municipality and\nnames one settlement of the 1910 Hungarian census, keyed by <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"gista\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">GISta Hungarorum</a>'s <code>IDTel1910</code>, or refuses it with a\nreason. Every in-scope birth is linked or refused, never guessed.</p></div><nav class=\"toc\"><span>On this page</span><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-where-it-stands\">Where it stands</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-the-district-step\">The district step</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-scope\">Scope</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-the-gazetteer\">The gazetteer</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-the-link-in-order\">The link, in order</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-refusals-and-the-queue\">Refusals and the queue</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-the-repairs-in-records-geo-hu-the-link-rests-on\">The repairs in records_geo_hu the link rests on</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-what-it-is-not\">What it is not</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-known-residuals-low-with-counts-the-stopping-rule-no-medium-or-high-finding-left\">Known residuals (low, with counts; the stopping rule: no medium or high finding left)</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-where-the-link-sits-now-the-canonical-birthplace-d-261\">Where the link sits now — the canonical birthplace (D-261)</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-open-for-the-author\">Open for the author</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-code-outputs-and-checks\">Code, outputs and checks</a><a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-how-we-got-here\">How we got here</a></nav>\n<p>This is the replicator's detail behind <a href=\"#places\">Birthplace</a>, whose top holds the method and the open\nrulings of both countries. The link is the Transleithanian counterpart of the <a href=\"#birth-settlement\">Czech settlement\nlink</a> (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-241\">D-241</a>). Decisions: <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-19\">D-19</a> to <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-22\">D-22</a> for the district step, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-256\">D-256</a> to <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-259\">D-259</a> and <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-262\">D-262</a> for\nthe link (<a href=\"#decisions\"><code>DECISIONS.md</code></a>); the checks: <a href=\"#validation-register\"><code>VALIDATION.md</code></a>; the code:\n<a href=\"#pipeline\"><code>PIPELINE.md</code></a>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-where-it-stands\">Where it stands</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The module.</strong> <code>birth_settlement_sk</code> 1.3.0, on the járás repairs of\n  <code>records_geo_hu</code> 1.6.0. Notebook 02 <strong>§4c</strong> writes its columns onto both person\n  files, and the gazetteer to <code>data/final/geo/settlements_gista_1910</code> (key <code>idtel</code>; 4,873\n  settlements).</li>\n<li><strong>In <code>data/final</code></strong> (the person files of 2026-11-21): <strong>9,332</strong> legionnaires and\n  <strong>19,809</strong> fallen Habsburg soldiers carry a 1910 GISta settlement (<code>birth_settlement_sk_id</code>).\n  2,192 and 6,132 of them are flagged <code>birth_settlement_sk_uncertain</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Where the numbers below come from:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>R</strong> = <code>output/places_sk/birth_settlement_sk_report.json</code>, the build report of <code>birth_settlement_sk</code>\n  1.1.0 (written 2026-11-18).</li>\n<li><strong>M</strong> = <code>output/places_sk/measure_sk_1.1.0.json</code> (measurement 1.4.0). It reads the frames as notebook 02 §4\n  reads them, <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> re-parsed from the raw cell, so the as-is notebook frame differs from it by a few rows.</li>\n<li><strong>Hand counts</strong> are one-off reads by checker sessions, labelled so.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The table is read from R <code>coverage</code> (= M <code>links_shipped</code>) when this page is built:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Legion</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>In scope</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">11,572</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">23,062</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Linked</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">9,090 (78.5 %)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">19,735 (85.6 %)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>of which certain</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">7,140</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">13,674</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>of which uncertain</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,950</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6,061</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>járás corrected (same county only)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,019</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,643</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>linked with no unit (a C3 county-only village)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">112</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">411</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Refused</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,482</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,327</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><em>Uncertain</em> is the OR of nine components, each its own column <code>birth_settlement_sk_&lt;component&gt;</code>. A link can carry\nseveral. The counts are read from the person files and equal R <code>coverage</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Component</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Legion</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>accent_only</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">937</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,934</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>source_question</code> (the source's \"?\")</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">82</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,335</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>mai_nev_only</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">58</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">485</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fuzzy</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">801</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">462</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>partial_name</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">127</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>name_conflict</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">27</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>border</code> (from 1.1.0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">218</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">732</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>sound</code> (from 1.1.0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">137</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">222</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hungarian_several</code> (from 1.1.0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">52</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Subcarpathian settlements linked: 123 legion,\n3,235 <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-the-district-step\">The district step</h2>\n<p>Here the difficulty has nothing to do with time. In 1910 the official language was <strong>Hungarian</strong>, but the soldiers\nand the modern census speak <strong>Slovak</strong>: the GIS map says <em>Nyitra</em>, the record says <em>Nitra</em>; the map says\n<em>Érsekújvár</em>, the record says <em>Nové Zámky</em>. Every address is potentially in the \"wrong\" language.</p>\n<p>This side reads the <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"gista\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">GISta Hungarorum</a> backbone and the <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"majo_2012\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">Majo 2012</a> lexicon (<code>districts_hu.py</code> and <code>lexikon_sk.py</code>;\nsources #8–#9 in <a href=\"#sources\"><code>DATA_SOURCES.md</code></a>). It runs <strong>only on records the Czech frame left unplaced</strong>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"move-1-read-the-district-through-a-magyarslovak-dictionary\">Move 1 — read the district, through a Magyar↔Slovak dictionary</h3>\n<p>Match the record's district string to a district <strong>seat</strong> (Slovak name, curated onto the Magyar backbone). Else\nmatch just the <strong>county</strong> (megye), else a fuzzy spelling.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"c1\"># records_geo_hu.py · add_jaras_id  (core logic)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">hit</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">unit_lut</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>                    <span class=\"c1\"># 1. district SEAT (Slovak) -&gt; unit; tier \"jaras\" / \"town\"</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">hit</span> <span class=\"ow\">is</span> <span class=\"ow\">not</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">jid</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">tier</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">hit</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"o\">...</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ck</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">_county_key</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>                    <span class=\"c1\"># 2. county only -&gt; megye (no district), tier \"megye\"</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">ck</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">megye_lut</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">jid</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">tier</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">mid</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"megye\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">megye_lut</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ck</span><span class=\"p\">];</span> <span class=\"k\">continue</span>\n<span class=\"n\">bare</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">_RURAL_SUFFIX</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sub</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">strip</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># 3. \"kosice vonkov\" -&gt; \"kosice\"; by RULE, not by luck</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">bare</span> <span class=\"o\">!=</span> <span class=\"n\">k</span> <span class=\"ow\">and</span> <span class=\"n\">unit_lut</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bare</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">jid</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">tier</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">unit_lut</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">bare</span><span class=\"p\">];</span> <span class=\"k\">continue</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">fuzzy</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>                                <span class=\"c1\"># 4. close spelling</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">m</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">process</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extractOne</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">fkeys</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">scorer</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">fuzz</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">token_set_ratio</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">m</span> <span class=\"ow\">and</span> <span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">&gt;=</span> <span class=\"n\">threshold</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">best</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"n\">unit_lut</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">][</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">x</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">fkeys</span> <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">fuzz</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">token_set_ratio</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">]}</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"nb\">len</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">best</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>               <span class=\"c1\"># a tie means the cell names two districts -&gt; refuse</span>\n            <span class=\"n\">uid</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">unit_lut</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">]][</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">];</span> <span class=\"n\">tier</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"fuzzy\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"o\">...</span>\n</pre></div>\n\n<p>A tie at the fuzzy step is refused outright (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-22\">D-22</a>). The municipality could break only <strong>6</strong> of the 38 Slovak ties,\nagainst 224 on the Czech side, so a second mechanism would not pay for itself. That is measured, not assumed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-naming-trap-and-how-the-map-disarms-it\">The naming trap (and how the map disarms it)</h3>\n<p>Subtle, and worth understanding. The lexicon names a <em>district</em> in Slovak: \"okres Nové Zámky\". The GIS map stores\nthat same district under its Hungarian <strong>adjective</strong>, <code>jaras_hu = \"Érsekújvári\"</code>, and labels it with its <strong>seat\ntown</strong>, which is a <em>different place</em> (<code>name_sk = \"Šurany\"</code>).</p>\n<p>So \"Nové Zámky the district\" and \"Šurany the seat\" are one administrative unit wearing two unrelated names. A naive\nmatcher never connects them.</p>\n<p>The fix: <strong>the map already contains its own Magyar↔Slovak dictionary, for free.</strong> The chartered towns on the map\ncarry <em>both</em> names (Érsekújvár = Nové Zámky). So to name a district in Slovak, strip the Hungarian adjective\n(<code>Érsekújvári → Érsekújvár</code>) and look that town up in the map's own two-language town list: \"Nové Zámky\".</p>\n<p>For the last handful whose base town is not on the map, we asked <strong><a href=\"https://query.wikidata.org/\">Wikidata</a></strong> for the\nSlovak label and wrote the pairs into <code><code>district_sk_curation.csv</code></code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Fülek→Fiľakovo</code></li>\n<li><code>Párkány→Štúrovo</code></li>\n<li><code>Rimaszécs→Rimavská Seč</code></li>\n<li><code>Udvard→Dvory nad Žitavou</code></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"c1\"># lexikon_sk.py · build_crosswalk_sk  (core logic)</span>\n<span class=\"c1\"># the backbone's OWN Magyar-&gt;Slovak dictionary — chartered towns carry both names</span>\n<span class=\"n\">hu2sk</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"n\">_norm</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_hu\"</span><span class=\"p\">]):</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_sk\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">backbone_hu</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">iterrows</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n         <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_hu\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"ow\">and</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_sk\"</span><span class=\"p\">)}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">jar</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">iterrows</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">keys</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_sk\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_sk_alt\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_sk_modern\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"name_hu\"</span><span class=\"p\">]]</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">base</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">_hu_adj_base</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"jaras_hu\"</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>            <span class=\"c1\"># \"Érsekújvári\" -&gt; \"Érsekújvár\"</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">base</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">keys</span> <span class=\"o\">+=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">base</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">hu2sk</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">_norm</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">base</span><span class=\"p\">))]</span>    <span class=\"c1\"># + the district's SLOVAK name -&gt; \"Nové Zámky\"</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">nm</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">keys</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">seat_lut</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">setdefault</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">_norm</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"unit_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n</pre></div>\n\n<h3 id=\"move-2-drop-to-the-village-unambiguous-and-corroborated-only\">Move 2 — drop to the village, unambiguous and corroborated only</h3>\n<p>Villages resolve through the Majo obec crosswalk (<code>build_crosswalk_sk</code> above), matched on <code>birth_municipality</code>. The\npass runs <strong>only on rows the Czech frame left unplaced</strong> (<code>okres_id</code> empty): a Czech-placed record must never also\nacquire a Slovak district. It refuses rather than guesses, three ways:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"c1\"># records_geo_hu.py · add_settlement_jaras  (core logic)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">gate</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">jid_col</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isna</span><span class=\"p\">()</span> <span class=\"o\">&amp;</span> <span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">muni_col</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">notna</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">gate</span> <span class=\"o\">&amp;=</span> <span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">prefix</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">_okres_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isna</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>     <span class=\"c1\"># NEVER touch Czech-placed rows</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">units</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">name_units</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>                    <span class=\"c1\"># járás unit_id(s) for villages of this name</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">ok</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>                                       <span class=\"c1\"># record names a district -&gt; it MUST corroborate</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">units</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span> <span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">u</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">units</span> <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">ok</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">name_okres</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"p\">())}</span>   <span class=\"c1\"># okres_sk or župa</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"ow\">not</span> <span class=\"n\">units</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">continue</span>                             <span class=\"c1\"># contradicts every candidate -&gt; refuse</span>\n<span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>                                        <span class=\"c1\"># bare name -&gt; positive-signal rules</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">land</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">_VETO_LANDS</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">continue</span>                             <span class=\"c1\"># positively foreign (Galicia, Russia, ...) -&gt; refuse</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">land</span> <span class=\"o\">!=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"Slovakia\"</span> <span class=\"ow\">and</span> <span class=\"n\">k</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">exclude_names</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">continue</span>                             <span class=\"c1\"># name exists in the CZECH frame too -&gt; refuse</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"nb\">len</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">units</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">!=</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">continue</span>                                 <span class=\"c1\"># ambiguous -&gt; leave &lt;NA&gt;, DO NOT guess</span>\n</pre></div>\n\n<h3 id=\"cross-frame-homonyms-the-praha-problem\">Cross-frame homonyms — the \"Praha problem\"</h3>\n<p>The same village name can exist in <strong>both</strong> countries: the hamlet <em>Praha</em> in okres Lučenec against the capital;\n<em>Petrovice</em>, <em>Čechy</em>, <em>Teplá</em>, …. A bare municipality with no district text gives <strong>no way to tell which country's\nplace is meant</strong>.</p>\n<p>So neither side's bare-name tier may claim a name that appears in the other side's frame (<code>exclude_names</code> above).\nThe Czech <code>muni</code> tier symmetrically refuses names present in the Slovak obec list.</p>\n<p>The only overrides are <em>positive</em> signals:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a district string that corroborates one side;</li>\n<li>a <code>land</code> already positively classified, \"Slovakia\" via the curated district list, so a bare <em>Košice</em> keeps its\n  Slovak match.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Everything else stays <code>&lt;NA&gt;</code>: an unknowable address is left unmatched, not guessed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"a-seat-that-is-also-a-country-halic\">A seat that is also a country — Halič</h3>\n<p><strong>Halič</strong> is a small Novohrad town (Hungarian <em>Gács</em>) and the seat of a járás, and it is also the Czech name for\n<strong>Galicia</strong>. The seat is therefore <strong>never resolved from the district string</strong> (<code>_AMBIGUOUS_SEATS</code> in\n<code>records_geo_hu</code>, exact, strip and fuzzy steps alike). A genuine Halič birth still resolves through the settlement\npass, whose municipality must be corroborated. What the rule repaired is under <a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-how-we-got-here\">How we got\nhere</a>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"land-and-the-cisleithanian-flag-follow-the-placement\">Land and the Cisleithanian flag follow the placement</h3>\n<p><code>set_land_from_jaras</code> sets <em>Slovakia</em> wherever a járás is set. A járás is a Slovak unit, so this is a definition,\nnot an inference.</p>\n<p>The remaining text markers are matched as <strong>whole country nouns</strong>. As substrings they had put <em>Polská Ostrava</em> in\nPoland, <em>Nemecká Ľupča</em> in Germany, <em>Kapušany</em> overseas (\"usa\") and <em>Ruskov</em> in Russia.</p>\n<p><code>sync_cisleithanian</code> derives the <code>*_cisleithanian</code> flag from the land after every land update, and the QA gate\nasserts both directions.</p>\n<h3 id=\"jaras-and-town-twins-the-same-convention-and-a-census-that-can-split-them\">Járás and town twins — the same convention, and a census that <em>can</em> split them</h3>\n<p>Twenty-six seats in Upper Hungary name <strong>two</strong> units: the járás, and the chartered town (<em>rendezett tanácsú</em> /\n<em>törvényhatósági város</em>) at its centre. The town sat administratively <strong>outside</strong> the district it gave its name to:\nBratislava, Košice, Nitra, Prešov, Žilina, Trenčín, Zvolen, Banská Bystrica and eighteen more. This is the\nadministration as it was, structurally the same problem as the Czech <code>X</code> / <code>X (město)</code> pairs.</p>\n<p>The rules are the Czech ones, deliberately (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-19\">D-19</a>):</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>A bare district name means the járás.</strong> It is the larger unit and it is what the string actually names. The\n   lookup says so outright rather than inheriting the order <code>sort_values(\"unit_type\")</code> happened to produce.</li>\n<li><strong>A trailing rural qualifier is stripped by rule.</strong> <code>Košice vonkov</code>, <code>Bratislava - venkov</code>, <code>Košice-okolí)</code> all\n   mean the ring, and they resolve at <code>jaras</code>. The same regex serves both countries (<code>records_geo._RURAL_SUFFIX</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>The municipality picks the member.</strong> A chartered town was one municipality, so this is a definition and not an\n   inference.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>A record with no municipality at all goes to the járás, flagged <code>undecided</code> in <code>birth_jaras_twin</code>; the counts are on\n<a href=\"#places-reading-the-output--the-match-tier-column\">Birthplace</a>. When the rule came in (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-19\">D-19</a>, 2026-08-01),\n<strong>1,888 records moved</strong> to a town unit (729 legion / 1,159 <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a>) and <strong>71</strong> had no municipality.</p>\n<h4 id=\"why-there-is-no-pooled-unit-here\">Why there is no pooled unit here</h4>\n<p>This is the one place the two countries genuinely diverge, and it is worth stating plainly so the asymmetry does not\nread as an oversight. The Czech twins had to be <strong>pooled</strong> (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-18\">D-18</a>), because a\n<em>Statutarstadt</em> had no Gerichtsbezirk of its own and the court-level workbooks keep a single row for the pair: the\nsource cannot make the split.</p>\n<p>The Hungarian census can. The GISta járás panel carries a separate row for <strong>all 192 backbone units</strong>, both members\nof every one of the 26 pairs included. So there is no <code>census_okres_id</code> equivalent on the Slovak side, no counts to\nsum and no shares to re-derive.</p>\n<p>Assignment is the whole problem, and both members keep their own covariates, which is what makes it worth getting\nright:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>pair</th>\n<th>Slovak share, ring</th>\n<th>Slovak share, town</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Žilina</td>\n<td>0.964</td>\n<td>0.540</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Prešov</td>\n<td>0.846</td>\n<td>0.398</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bratislava</td>\n<td>0.633 (Magyar 0.136)</td>\n<td>0.149 (Magyar 0.405)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3 id=\"the-lexicons-own-two-traps\">The lexicón's own two traps</h3>\n<p>The Majo lexicon prints its block headers in more than one wording, and the reader matches every one of them (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-20\">D-20</a>,\n<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-21\">D-21</a>):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>town blocks</strong>: four wordings, the plural <code>mestá so zriadeným magistrátom</code> among them;</li>\n<li><strong>okres blocks</strong>: <code>okres X</code> <strong>and</strong> the adjectival <code>X okres</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A missed header does not fail loudly. The town blocks trail each county, so the rows keep the last-seen okres, land\nin the right county and look entirely plausible. What the two traps cost before they were found is under <a href=\"#birth-settlement-sk-how-we-got-here\">How we got\nhere</a>.</p>\n<p>The Majo tables are read with word <strong>x-coordinates</strong>, because zero columns are unprinted and text order alone\nmis-assigns the mother-tongue counts. The columns are <strong>right-aligned</strong> while the header anchors are their <em>left</em>\nedges, so each number is bucketed by its <strong>right</strong> edge (<code>lexikon_sk._read_numbers</code>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-scope\">Scope</h2>\n<p><strong>In scope</strong> is a birth with a <code>birth_jaras_id</code>. So are the villages C3 takes off a chartered town with no járás\naround it (Komárom, Nová Baňa, Banská Štiavnica while its ruling is open): county only, tier <code>megye</code>.</p>\n<p>Every in-scope birth is <strong>linked or refused with a reason</strong>, never both, never neither. This is asserted in §4c and\nby the §6 gate (<code>data_checks</code> 1.37.0; R <code>scope_without_reason</code> = 0, <code>refusal_carries_settlement</code> = 0).</p>\n<p><strong>No birth holds both a Czech and a Slovak settlement.</strong> The Czech link refuses a birth the Transleithanian frame\nowns (<code>transleithanian_frame</code>, Q1, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-245\">D-245</a>), and the gate checks it (HARD).</p>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-the-gazetteer\">The gazetteer</h2>\n<p><strong>4,873 settlements</strong>: every settlement of a backbone unit\n(4,868) plus every settlement today in Ukraine\n(504 Subcarpathian; R <code>gazetteer</code>).</p>\n<p>GISta gives, for each settlement:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the 1912 Hungarian name, today's name and country (<code>MAI NEV</code>, <code>MAI ORSZAG</code>);</li>\n<li>the 1900 and 1904–14 variants;</li>\n<li>the centre point, and the 1910 population and mother tongue.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Slovak names the records use come from <strong><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"majo_2012\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">Majo 2012</a></strong> (<code>lexikon_sk</code>). The join is <strong>one to one</strong> and always on a\nname <em>and</em> a second fact, never on <code>MAI NEV</code> alone, which is today's municipality and repeats across a merger.</p>\n<p><strong>3,467 of 3,511</strong>\nMajo rows join (R <code>majo_join</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Join tier</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Rows</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>name_pop</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,283</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>pop_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">104</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>name_pop_any_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">44</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>part_parent_pop</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">31</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>town_1912</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>swap_pop</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>The 44 left out carry a reason (R <code>majo_join.gaps</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Reason</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Rows</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>mai_nev_alone_population_differs</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">21</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>no_unit_and_no_name_population_match</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>name_not_in_unit_population_not_unique</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>majo_label_swap</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>A name-versus-population conflict stays unjoined</strong> rather than decided by rule, because either source can hold the\nswapped label. Of the 7 reciprocal crosswise <code>MAI NEV</code> pairs only <em>Plavecký Mikuláš</em> / <em>Peter</em> is GISta's swap\n(<code>gista_mai_nev_swaps</code>); that pair joins crosswise on the population, tier <code>swap_pop</code>. The other six are Majo's\npopulations. <code>majo_label_swaps</code> flags four Majo pairs whose 1910.1 labels the 1880–1900 rows contradict\n(<em>Andrejová</em> / <em>Ondrašovce</em> …).</p>\n<p><strong>Two overrides.</strong> GISta's <code>MAI ORSZAG</code> puts 13 Majo-joined settlements abroad (<em>Kremnica</em>, <em>Kľak</em> …): the link reads\nthem as Slovakia and keeps GISta's value in <code>mai_orszag_gista</code> (<code>gista_mai_orszag_overrides</code>). And a Majo-joined\nsettlement's <code>MAI NEV</code> is a name form too when it differs from the Majo name and names no other settlement of the\ncounty (<em>Dubnica nad Váhom</em>, <em>Lopej</em>; <code>mai_nev_joined</code>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-the-link-in-order\">The link, in order</h2>\n<p>In order (<code>link_one</code>; every rule a switch in <code>birth_settlement_sk.RULES</code>):</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Cell splitting.</strong> <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a>: the Slovak head and the Hungarian parenthetical, label words (<em>dříve:</em>, <em>dříve též</em> …)\n   stripped. Legion: the head, then the pieces split on brackets, <code>/</code>, <code>=</code> and a spaced hyphen.</li>\n<li><strong>An exact name inside the unit</strong> (<code>exact_unit</code>; a Hungarian form <code>exact_unit_hungarian</code>), or the Hungarian\n   parenthetical inside the unit or the county (<code>hungarian_unit</code>, <code>hungarian_county</code>). <em>X Svätý Y</em> also reads <em>X Y</em>\n   (<code>saint_drop</code>).</li>\n<li><strong><code>prefix_unit</code></strong>: the record names only the head of one <code>&lt;name&gt; nad/pod/pri …</code> or double-name settlement of the\n   unit (<em>Stráže</em> → <em>Stráže nad Myjavou</em>), or its one <code>&lt;county adjective&gt; &lt;name&gt;</code> (<em>Porúbka</em> → <em>Liptovská\n   Porúbka</em>). Two candidates refuse (<code>ambiguous_in_unit</code>). Uncertain (<code>partial_name</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>A name unique in another járás of the same county</strong> (<code>name_county</code>): <code>birth_jaras_corrected</code> = True.\n   <code>birth_jaras_id</code>, the written key, is never changed; the HU census key <code>birth_census_jaras_id</code> follows the link\n   (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-262\">D-262</a>). Across a county line only into a bordering járás (step 7).</li>\n<li><strong><code>town_city</code></strong>: a birth records_geo_hu put on a chartered town because its municipality is the town takes the\n   town's one settlement (<em>Banská Štiavnica a Banská Belá</em>).</li>\n<li><strong>Near name</strong> (rapidfuzz ≥ 85, one candidate, no exact namesake anywhere): <code>fuzzy_unit</code>. For a birth with <strong>no</strong>\n   unit (a C3 county-only village), the county's one (<code>fuzzy_county</code>, never a settlement today in Hungary). Always\n   uncertain. Three refusals guard it:<ul>\n<li>a containing name sharing a word of five letters is a competitor (<code>fuzzy_contained</code>: <em>Šutovce</em> is not\n  <em>Súlovce</em> while <em>Dolné / Horné Šútovce</em> exist — <code>ambiguous_in_county</code>);</li>\n<li>a name of adjectives alone takes no near name (<em>Horné</em>, <em>Spišský</em>);</li>\n<li>a near name the cell's Hungarian name contradicts is refused <code>cross_county_unique</code> (<em>Malé Rátovce (Kis-Rát)</em>).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>1.1.0, the author's rulings of 2026-11-18.</strong> Each is uncertain and a switch in <code>RULES_110</code>; all off = 1.0.3, 0\n   rows differ (M <code>link_rules_110_off_vs_1_0_3_rows_differing</code>). The rulings are below the list.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><code>border_unit</code></strong> (S1, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-257\">D-257</a> amended; the author: \"yes\"). A <code>cross_county_unique</code> candidate links when its járás\nshares a stretch of boundary with the stated one (GISta <code>MO_JarasVaros</code> polygons, two or more shared vertices on a\n25 m grid; <code>jaras_borders</code>), <code>birth_jaras_corrected</code> = True, component <code>border</code>. Never on a cell whose Hungarian name\npoints elsewhere (<code>hungarian_names_another</code>), never on a birth with no unit. A cell whose county words name a third\ncounty keeps the queue row.</p>\n<p>Then, only on a <code>not_found</code> (S2, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-256\">D-256</a> extended), four tiers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>sound_unit</code> / <code>sound_county</code>.</strong> On a coarse sound key the names name one settlement of the whole gazetteer,\n  inside the unit / the county (<em>Takšoň</em> = Taksonyfalva, <em>Peštěn</em> = Pöstyén). The key: Hungarian <em>cs</em>, <em>cz</em>, <em>ch</em> =\n  č, <em>sz</em> = s, <em>s</em> = š, <em>gy</em> = ď, <em>ny</em> = ň, <em>ly</em> = j, <em>ty</em> = ť, <em>ö</em> = e, <em>ü</em> = u, <em>y</em> = i; accents and spaces\n  dropped.</li>\n<li><strong><code>hungarian_in_unit</code></strong>: the cell's Hungarian name names several settlements of the county and one of the unit\n  (<em>Ilnice (Iloncza)</em>).</li>\n<li><strong><code>hyphen_part</code></strong>: a <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> <em>A-B</em> where Majo's 1910.2 gives <em>B</em> as a part of <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> names one settlement of the\n  unit (<em>Liptovský Svätý Mikuláš-Vrbica</em>).</li>\n<li><strong><code>sound_near_unit</code></strong>: the unit's one near name on the sound key (≥ 85), none elsewhere in the county, no\n  containing sound key of five letters or more in the county, never adjectives alone.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Two of them naming two settlements refuse (<code>ambiguous_in_county</code>). Not built, by ruling: a namesake beside the\nborder, <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a>'s head county.</p>\n<h3 id=\"tier-counts\">Tier counts</h3>\n<p>R <code>by_tier</code>; a dash where a run has none.</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tier</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Legion</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>exact_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6,049</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">11,532</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hungarian_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,907</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hungarian_county</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,991</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>name_county</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,863</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,313</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>border_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">217</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">729</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>exact_unit_hungarian</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">248</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">688</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fuzzy_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">434</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">222</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>sound_near_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">103</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">159</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>prefix_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">112</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">29</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>sound_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">11</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">52</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hungarian_in_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">52</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hyphen_part</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">21</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>sound_county</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">23</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">11</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fuzzy_county</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">23</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>town_city</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">19</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3 id=\"how-the-110-tiers-were-checked\">How the 1.1.0 tiers were checked</h3>\n<p>The 1.1.0 tiers add 354 legion and 1,024 <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> links (R). They were read by hand in two steps (the one-off read of\n2026-11-18, seed 21):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>First read</strong>: 40 <code>border_unit</code>, 40 <code>sound_unit</code>/<code>sound_county</code>, 40 <code>sound_near_unit</code>, 40 <code>hungarian_in_unit</code>\n  (all <em>Ilnice</em>, the one place the tier reaches), and all 21 <code>hyphen_part</code>: 0 wrong of 181.</li>\n<li><strong>To the size that certifies a 6 % bar</strong>, the two large tiers (with no wrong row a Wilson 95 % upper bound under\n  6 % needs 61 rows; the same seed, so the first 40 are the rows above): <code>border_unit</code> 0 wrong of 61 and\n  <code>sound_near_unit</code> 0 wrong of 61, no doubtful row, upper bound 0.059 each.</li>\n<li><strong>The smaller tiers</strong> keep their 40-row reads (<code>sound_unit</code>/<code>sound_county</code>, 0.088; <code>hungarian_in_unit</code>, 0.088)\n  and their whole-tier read (<code>hyphen_part</code>, 21 rows, a population count).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-refusals-and-the-queue\">Refusals and the queue</h2>\n<h3 id=\"cross-county-refusal-d-257\">Cross-county refusal (D-257)</h3>\n<p>The district string is the <em>interwar</em> okres, which spans two 1910 counties around Parkan, Želiezovce, Šaľa and\nModrý Kameň. A name found only in another county therefore links only where the candidate's járás <strong>borders</strong> the\nstated one (<code>border_unit</code>, step 7): uncertain and corrected.</p>\n<p>What stays <strong>refused and queued</strong> as <code>cross_county_unique</code>\n(299 legion,\n192 <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a>):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a birth with no unit;</li>\n<li>a candidate beyond the border;</li>\n<li>a cell whose two names point two ways.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The queue says how the cell's Hungarian name bears on the candidate: <code>hungarian_corroborates</code>, <code>hungarian_only</code>,\n<code>hungarian_picks_namesake</code> or <code>hungarian_names_another</code>.</p>\n<p><strong><code>county_fuzzy_any</code></strong> gives a birth with a unit the county's near name in another unit. It is <strong>on</strong> since 1.3.0\n(<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-284\">D-284</a>; the author, 2026-11-21: \"Link, flagged\"): the link's tier is <code>fuzzy_county</code>, so it is always\n<code>birth_settlement_sk_uncertain</code> and a strict run leaves it out. From 1.0.3 to 1.2.1 it was off and its pick was\nrefused as <code>county_fuzzy_ruling</code>. Switched on it links 241 / 71 (M <code>link_rules.shipped_plus</code>, the measure of\n2026-11-18). The checkers' one-off read of 30 + 30 queued picks: legion 24 right, 5\ndoubtful, 1 likely wrong; <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> 25 right, 4 doubtful, 1 wrong.</p>\n<p><strong>The queue</strong>, <code>output/places_sk/birth_settlement_sk_rulings_queue.csv</code>, holds <strong>823 rows</strong> (R\n<code>rulings_queue_rows</code>). It holds those two reasons plus <code>hungarian_name_disagrees</code>\n(3 /\n18). Each row carries the refused candidate, its\ndistance from the unit and (40 rows) the one in-unit settlement whose Slovak name ends or starts with the record's\nname.</p>\n<h3 id=\"other-refusals\">Other refusals</h3>\n<p>R; a dash where a run has none.</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Refusal</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Legion</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>not_found</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,789</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,352</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ambiguous_vua_candidates</code> (<a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a>'s cell holds several candidates)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,548</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ambiguous_outside_county</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">89</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">34</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>no_municipality</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">30</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">88</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ambiguous_in_county</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">22</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ambiguous_in_unit</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">8</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">–</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>county_words_disagree</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">15</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>region_words_disagree</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>another_land</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3 id=\"guards\">Guards</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>County words</strong> left in a cell must name the settlement's county.</li>\n<li><strong>A land word</strong> (<em>Morava</em>, <em>Solnohrad</em>, <em>Čechy</em>) refuses unless it is the record's own municipality or carries a\n  <code>?</code>. A bare <em>Halič</em> is the Novohrad járás only in Nógrád (Galicia otherwise).</li>\n<li><strong>A region word</strong> (<em>Slovensko</em>, <em>Podkarpatská Rus</em>) refuses only a cell whose own district string resolved no unit,\n  and <em>Podkarpatská Rus</em> accepts a settlement of Ung.</li>\n<li><strong>A Hungarian name found outside the unit</strong> does not link when the Slovak name names one other settlement of the\n  county (<code>hungarian_name_disagrees</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"dd-sk\">Refusals of the Slovak settlement link, by reason: open a sample</h3><p class=\"note\">Read from the person files in <code>data/final</code> (<code>birth_settlement_sk_refusal</code>). Click a count for up to 20 of its records, drawn with seed 1910 so the sample holds from build to build: the record id, the place strings as written and what the link refused. Never a name.</p><div class=\"ixbar ddbar\" data-ix=\"dd-sk\" data-rows=\"11\"></div><div class=\"tblwrap\"><table class=\"tbl ddtable\"><thead><tr><th>Reason</th><th>Legion</th><th>VÚA</th><th>All</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>not_found</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-not_found\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">1,788</button></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-not_found\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">1,352</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"3140\">3,140</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_vua_candidates</code></td><td class=\"num\">–</td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-ambiguous_vua_candidates\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">1,548</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"1548\">1,548</td></tr><tr><td><code>cross_county_unique</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-cross_county_unique\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">298</button></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-cross_county_unique\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">189</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"487\">487</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_outside_county</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-ambiguous_outside_county\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">89</button></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-ambiguous_outside_county\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">34</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"123\">123</td></tr><tr><td><code>no_municipality</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-no_municipality\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">30</button></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-no_municipality\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">88</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"118\">118</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_in_county</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-ambiguous_in_county\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">22</button></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-ambiguous_in_county\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">3</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"25\">25</td></tr><tr><td><code>hungarian_name_disagrees</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-hungarian_name_disagrees\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">3</button></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-hungarian_name_disagrees\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">18</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"21\">21</td></tr><tr><td><code>county_words_disagree</code></td><td class=\"num\">–</td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-county_words_disagree\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">15</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"15\">15</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_in_unit</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-ambiguous_in_unit\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">8</button></td><td class=\"num\">–</td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"8\">8</td></tr><tr><td><code>another_land</code></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-legion-another_land\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">2</button></td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-another_land\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">3</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"5\">5</td></tr><tr><td><code>region_words_disagree</code></td><td class=\"num\">–</td><td class=\"num\"><button class=\"ddbtn\" data-dd=\"sk-vua-region_words_disagree\" onclick=\"ddOpen(this)\" title=\"Show up to 20 sampled records\">3</button></td><td class=\"num\" data-s=\"3\">3</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"ddpanel\" hidden></div><details class=\"ixtwin\"><summary>The counts as a plain table</summary><div class=\"tblwrap\"><table class=\"tbl\" data-static-for=\"dd-sk\" data-rows=\"11\"><thead><tr><th>Reason</th><th>Legion</th><th>VÚA</th><th>All</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>not_found</code></td><td class=\"num\">1,788</td><td class=\"num\">1,352</td><td class=\"num\">3,140</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_vua_candidates</code></td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">1,548</td><td class=\"num\">1,548</td></tr><tr><td><code>cross_county_unique</code></td><td class=\"num\">298</td><td class=\"num\">189</td><td class=\"num\">487</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_outside_county</code></td><td class=\"num\">89</td><td class=\"num\">34</td><td class=\"num\">123</td></tr><tr><td><code>no_municipality</code></td><td class=\"num\">30</td><td class=\"num\">88</td><td class=\"num\">118</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_in_county</code></td><td class=\"num\">22</td><td class=\"num\">3</td><td class=\"num\">25</td></tr><tr><td><code>hungarian_name_disagrees</code></td><td class=\"num\">3</td><td class=\"num\">18</td><td class=\"num\">21</td></tr><tr><td><code>county_words_disagree</code></td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">15</td><td class=\"num\">15</td></tr><tr><td><code>ambiguous_in_unit</code></td><td class=\"num\">8</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">8</td></tr><tr><td><code>another_land</code></td><td class=\"num\">2</td><td class=\"num\">3</td><td class=\"num\">5</td></tr><tr><td><code>region_words_disagree</code></td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">3</td><td class=\"num\">3</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-the-repairs-in-records-geo-hu-the-link-rests-on\">The repairs in <code>records_geo_hu</code> the link rests on</h2>\n<p>Each repair is a switch. All off gives 1.4.2; 1.5.3 with C3q and S2g off and the ruling kept gives 1.5.2 (0 rows\neach, M).</p>\n<p>Birth role, cumulative rows changed, legion / <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> (M <code>repairs.birth.cumulative</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Repair</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Rows</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>C3</strong></td>\n<td>a town-named interwar okres → the járás around the town (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-259\">D-259</a>)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">763 / 1,619</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>C3n</strong></td>\n<td>the joined town <em>Banská Štiavnica a Banská Belá</em></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5 / 44</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>C3q</strong></td>\n<td>a <code>?</code> compound is undecided, a hyphen tail is checked: <em>Nová Baňa-Svätý Kríž</em> is not the town</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0 / 2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>S2</strong></td>\n<td>the district string read piece by piece, tier <code>settlement_fuzzy</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">684 / 1,167</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>S2b</strong></td>\n<td>a positively foreign land stops S2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2 / 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>S2f</strong></td>\n<td>pieces naming two units: the county where they share one, tier <code>frame</code>, land Slovakia</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">29 / 1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>S2g</strong></td>\n<td>S2f keeps the land only when every piece is in the frame</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0 / 0 birth, 5 / 0 home</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>C7</strong> (the land label <em>Subcarpathia</em>, 248 / 3,349 rows) is built and <strong>off</strong> (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-258\">D-258</a>).</p>\n<p>With the repairs off the link reaches 8,384 / 17,753 births, with them 8,736 / 18,711 (M <code>links_repairs_off</code>,\n<code>links_repairs_on</code>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-what-it-is-not\">What it is not</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A link says the <em>string</em> names that settlement</strong>; the Habsburg-army side does not check it.</li>\n<li><strong>GISta has no German names</strong>, and old Slovak forms of Hungarian names (<em>Urmín</em>, <em>Šandorf</em>) stay <code>not_found</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Majo covers present-day Slovakia only</strong>, so Subcarpathian villages link mostly through the <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> cell's Hungarian\n  name.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-known-residuals-low-with-counts-the-stopping-rule-no-medium-or-high-finding-left\">Known residuals (low, with counts; the stopping rule: no medium or high finding left)</h2>\n<p>From the checkers' reads of 1.0.2 and 1.0.3 (one-off) and the 1.0.3 fix round:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Near-name picks queued, not linked.</strong> About 10 doubtful or wrong among the 60 <code>county_fuzzy_ruling</code> picks read\n  (above). One doubtful <code>mai_nev_joined</code> link (<em>Horné Zariečie</em> → <em>Záriečie</em>, legion).</li>\n<li><strong>The county adjective and the reverse <em>nad/pod</em> suffix are not generalised.</strong> The bare name the unit holds once\n  after a county adjective (<em>Polhora</em> ×4, <em>Biskupice</em>, <em>Nová Ves</em> ×2, <em>Bystrica</em>, <em>Krásna Hôrka</em>, <em>Vysoká</em> ×4) is\n  refused or queued with a farther candidate; the queue carries the near candidate on 40 rows. Reverse suffix: 2\n  legion rows (50484, 105132). <code>prefix_heads</code> costs 2 legion links.</li>\n<li><strong>Piece readings of S2</strong> are wrong on 13 legion / 1 <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> rows. Legion 7650 is in the wrong járás with the right\n  settlement; <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> 8170 and 48485 as read at 1.0.2.</li>\n<li><strong>Subcarpathian frame rows.</strong> An S2f row whose every unit is Subcarpathian keeps land Slovakia (2 legion births).\n  With C7 off every Subcarpathian birth does (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-258\">D-258</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>Interwar okresy across two counties</strong> (Parkan, Želiezovce, Šaľa, Modrý Kameň) are not marked county-unsure. Their\n  cross-county names link only into a bordering járás (<code>border_unit</code>, uncertain); the rest are queued.</li>\n<li><strong>1.1.0 against its sizing</strong> (the analyst's, 2026-11-18):<ul>\n<li><code>border_unit</code> <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> 729 of 735 (4 <code>hungarian_names_another</code> rows left out by the rule, 2 refused by the cell's\n  county words and kept in the queue);</li>\n<li><code>sound_near_unit</code> 103 / 159 of 117 / 162 (the containing-key competitor and the adjective guard);</li>\n<li><code>hyphen_part</code> 21 of 26 (5 rows whose <em>B</em> lies in another unit of the county: the ruling reads <em>of the unit</em>).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Unrecovered refusals</strong> listed at 1.0.2 that 1.0.3 did not reach. The rest are now linked or queued: <em>Plavecký</em>,\n  <em>Dubnica</em>, <em>Lopej</em>, <em>Ivánka</em>, <em>Savčina</em>, <em>Veľké Košecké Podhradie</em>, <em>Vyšný Olčvar</em>, <em>Dolný Ňáražd</em>, <em>Jelšavská\n  Teplica</em>, <em>Dolný Almáš</em>, <em>Nižné Matiašovce</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-where-the-link-sits-now-the-canonical-birthplace-d-261\">Where the link sits now — the canonical birthplace (D-261)</h2>\n<p>The link is the first source of the one birthplace the analysis reads (<code>birth_place_*</code>, notebook 02 §4d,\n<code>utils/parsing/birthplace_canonical.py</code>). Where it links, <code>birth_place_jaras_id</code> and <code>birth_place_megye_id</code> are the\n<strong>settlement's</strong> unit and county, across the county line on a <code>border_unit</code> link, and the point is GISta's\nsettlement centre. Elsewhere they are <code>birth_jaras_id</code> / <code>birth_megye_id</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>The Hungarian census join follows the link</strong> as the Czech one does (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-262\">D-262</a>, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-247\">D-247</a>; the author: \"Try to mimic the\nCzech side as much as possible\"). <code>correct_census_jaras_id</code> (1.2.0, run in §4c after the link) writes\n<code>birth_census_jaras_id</code>: the settlement's unit where <code>birth_jaras_corrected</code> or where no járás was written, else\n<code>birth_jaras_id</code>. It keeps the written key in <code>birth_census_jaras_id_stated</code>; §4b merges on it, and the canonical\n<code>birth_place_census_jaras_id</code> equals it on every row.</p>\n<p>Re-keyed, legion / <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a>: 2,355 / 4,092. They are:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Re-keyed because</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">Legion</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>corrected inside the county</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,053</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>border_unit</code>, across the county line</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">218</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">732</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>a county-only birth that gains a census row</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">84</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">360</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>How far that moves the covariates is on <a href=\"#places-the-canonical-birthplace--settlement-first-the-district-step-as-the-fallback-d-261\">Birthplace</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-open-for-the-author\">Open for the author</h2>\n<p>Every open ruling, Slovak and Czech, is one list, in <a href=\"#places-open-for-the-author\">Birthplace</a>. On this\nside:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the <code>county_fuzzy_any</code> block (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-257\">D-257</a>): ruled on 2026-11-21, linked and flagged (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-284\">D-284</a>);</li>\n<li>the Banská Štiavnica surround (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-259\">D-259</a>): ruled on 2026-11-21, kept (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-285\">D-285</a>);</li>\n<li>the <em>Subcarpathia</em> label C7 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-258\">D-258</a>): ruled on 2026-11-21, switched on (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-286\">D-286</a>);</li>\n<li>the rulings queue (<code>output/places_sk/birth_settlement_sk_rulings_queue.csv</code>, 823 rows, R\n  <code>rulings_queue_rows</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-code-outputs-and-checks\">Code, outputs and checks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Module:</strong> <code>utils/parsing/birth_settlement_sk.py</code> (1.3.0; every rule a switch\n  in <code>RULES</code>). It rests on the repairs of <code>utils/parsing/records_geo_hu.py</code> and on Majo's sub-parts and earlier years\n  from <code>utils/parsing/lexikon_sk.py</code> (<code>parse_parts_sk</code>, <code>parse_earlier_years</code>). Run by notebook 02 §4c\n  (<code>build_gazetteer_sk</code> → <code>add_birth_settlement_sk_columns</code> on both frames). Per-module detail:\n  <a href=\"#pipeline\">Pipeline</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>The GISta tables:</strong> <code>utils/reference_tools/places/export_gista_settlements.py</code> (run once, Windows) reads GISta's\n  settlement database into <code>data/raw/census_hu/settlements_1910/</code>. The source is #8c in <a href=\"#sources\">Data\n  sources</a>, Majo #9.</li>\n<li><strong>Outputs:</strong> <code>output/places_sk/</code>: <code>birth_settlement_sk_report.{json,md}</code>, the link files\n  <code>birth_settlement_sk_links_{legion,vua}.parquet</code>, the rulings queue, <code>gazetteer_sk_1910.*</code> and the GISta name-swap\n  and country-override tables.</li>\n<li><strong>Measurement:</strong> <code>utils/reference_tools/places/measure_birth_settlement_sk.py</code> (1.4.0) →\n  <code>output/places_sk/measure_sk_1.1.0.json</code>: the repairs and the rules switched off one by one.</li>\n<li><strong>Checks:</strong> the QA gate (<code>data_checks</code> 1.40.0, <code>_birth_settlement_sk_checks</code>: a corrected birth stays in its county\n  unless it is a <code>border_unit</code> link), <code>tests/test_birth_settlement_sk.py</code>, and the checker sessions' hand reads\n  (<a href=\"#validation-register\">Validation register</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"birth-settlement-sk-how-we-got-here\">How we got here</h2>\n<p>What the rules above repaired, and how the link changed from version to version. Dated, and kept as it was recorded.</p>\n<p><strong>The page.</strong> This section was moved here on 2026-11-18 from <a href=\"#places\"><code>PLACE_MATCHING.md</code></a>, where it was\nthe section <em>The Slovak settlement link</em>. In the docs pass (2026-11-20) it became the folded <em>Slovakia</em> section of\n<em>Birthplace</em>, and the Slovak district step moved in from <code>PLACE_MATCHING.md</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Halič</strong> (<code>records_geo_hu</code> 1.4.0).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Resolved by name, the district string <code>Halič</code> put <strong>214</strong> legionnaires born in Lvov, Přemyšl, Kraków, Kolomyja and\n  Tarnopol into a Slovak járás (131 on the exact string, 83 on fuzzy strings like <code>Brody - Halič</code>).</li>\n<li>There they carried its census covariates although their own <code>birth_land</code> already said Galicia. Of the 218 records\n  in the unit, 4 were Slovak.</li>\n<li>After the fix the unit holds 7 legion births, none of them Galician.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-land-de\" data-gl=\"land\">Land</a> and the Cisleithanian flag.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>birth_land</code> is decided twice on the Czech side (before and after the settlement pass) and was never revisited once\n  the Slovak passes ran. So <strong>1,041 legion and 2,707 <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a></strong> births placed in a járás still had no land, and 237 and 17\n  more had whatever land their text markers guessed.</li>\n<li>The <code>*_cisleithanian</code> flag came from <code>locations.py</code>'s text-only land and was never re-derived after the land was\n  corrected.</li>\n<li><strong>2,270</strong> Czech-lands <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> births were flagged <em>not</em> Cisleithanian, 1,747 of them in okres Uherské Hradiště or\n  Uherský Brod, because the substring <code>uhersk</code> meant Hungary. And <strong>8,997</strong> Slovak births were flagged Cisleithanian.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>The járás and town twins</strong> were read the same careless way as the Czech pairs: <strong>12,760 records sat in a pair and\nonly 387 of them on a town</strong>. A trailing rural qualifier reached the ring <em>by luck</em>: token-set fuzzy dropped the\nextra token and scored 100. <strong>589 records</strong> were resolved at the <code>fuzzy</code> tier and were afterwards\nindistinguishable from a bare <code>Košice</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>The lexicón's own two traps.</strong> Both were found on 2026-08-01, and both were the same mistake: <strong>a regex narrower\nthan the printed page</strong> (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-20\">D-20</a>, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-21\">D-21</a>).</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>what the page prints</th>\n<th>what was matched</th>\n<th>cost</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>town block headers, four wordings incl. plural <code>mestá so zriadeným magistrátom</code></td>\n<td><code>^mesto so</code> only</td>\n<td><strong>27</strong> town rows kept the county's last járás — obec <code>Nitra</code> filed under okres <em>Nové Mesto nad Váhom</em>; 79 records to the wrong járás</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>okres headers, <code>okres X</code> <strong>and</strong> adjectival <code>X okres</code></td>\n<td><code>^okres</code> only</td>\n<td>19 Orava obce silently inherited járás <em>Trstená</em> instead of <em>Tvrdošín</em> (~98 records); 36 more left unmapped</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Bratislava's four towns escaped only because a <em>singular</em> header sat above them on the same page.</p>\n<p><strong>The Majo columns.</strong> Reading the centre of a number drifted narrow values one column left and could merge two of\nthem: Nitra's 9 Croats and 13 Serbs became <em>913 Serbs</em>. Bucketing by the right edge repaired 27 broken row sums and\n135 rows that reconciled while sitting under the wrong heading; no share-bearing column moved on any row.</p>\n<p><strong>The link, 1.0.2 to 1.1.0.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1.0.3</strong> joined the <em>Plavecký Mikuláš</em> / <em>Peter</em> pair crosswise on the population (tier <code>swap_pop</code>), made a\n  Majo-joined settlement's <code>MAI NEV</code> a name form (<code>mai_nev_joined</code>), added <code>saint_drop</code>, and added the three refusals\n  that guard the near name (step 6). It shipped the 1.0.2 rule <code>county_fuzzy_any</code> <strong>off</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>The cross-county queue.</strong> In 1.0.3 a name found only in another county was <strong>refused and queued</strong>:\n  <code>cross_county_unique</code> (legion 516, <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> 921). The author ruled on that queue on 2026-11-18 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-257\">D-257</a> amended): where the\n  candidate's járás <strong>borders</strong> the stated one it links, uncertain and corrected (<code>border_unit</code>, legion 217, <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> 729:\n  step 7); a birth with no unit, a candidate beyond the border, and a cell whose two names point two ways stay refused\n  and queued — <code>cross_county_unique</code> legion 299, <a class=\"cite\" data-ref=\"vua_db\" href=\"#references\" onclick=\"return bibGo(event)\">VÚA</a> 192 in 1.1.0.</li>\n<li><strong>The queue</strong> held 1,769 rows in 1.0.3; the 946 rows gone are all <code>border_unit</code> links, none added.</li>\n<li><strong><code>not_found</code></strong> was 1,926 / 1,647 in 1.0.3, before the four 1.1.0 tiers that read it.</li>\n<li><strong>1.2.0</strong> added <code>correct_census_jaras_id</code> (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-262\">D-262</a>, the author's ruling of 2026-11-18), so the HU census key follows\n  the link.</li>\n</ul></div>");
